{{!--
  Dragonbane — ONE cell of the stat box.

  Called 24 times from front.hbs, once per row and column:

      {{> stat-cell for="front-stat-1a"}}

  The place's name arrives as the hash parameter `for` and so lands in the
  partial's context, where the helpers read it as a path. It is called `for`
  and not `slot` because a helper carries that name: a bare {{slot}} would
  call the helper, which then renders nothing. A name that works in only
  one of two positions is a trap, not a shortcut.

  `glyph=true`: a stored abbreviation prints in full when the card type
  declares a table for the cell (`Griff: 1H` → „einhändig"), and passes
  through when it does not. `markdown=false`: a value shows its link styled
  and nothing else reinterpreted.

  Deliberately one line: the hulls stand with their content on one line and
  are therefore not "standalone" for Handlebars, so the calling line's
  indentation is kept.
--}}
{{#if (slot for)}}<span class="db-stat">{{#if (slot-label for)}}<span class="db-stat-label">{{slot-label for}}</span> {{/if}}{{slot for markdown=false glyph=true}}</span>{{/if}}
